Per-task browser contexts (hyperhermes). With managed persistence every task
of a profile drove ONE Camofox userId, i.e. one Firefox context: parallel
delegate_task children and cron runs shared cookies, storage and logins with
each other and with the agent's own sessions. A child or cron task now gets
`<profile userId>-task-<digest>` (camofox_client.get_session), deleted with its
persisted state when the task ends (a subagent's or cron run's turn end:
cleanup_task(final=True) -> close_owned_contexts; a top-level session's own
contexts are left to the server's idle close and stale-state sweep); the
agent's own sessions keep the profile context (their logins), each with its
own tabs. browser_context (./camofox_extras.py)
switches a task explicitly ('shared' = the agent's logins, 'own'); the
config key browser.camofox.task_contexts: shared turns it off. Tabs and refs
were already per task (session key per task_id). Applies after
register-extras.patch, native-vision.patch and vault-frames.patch; targets the
official plugin at hermes v0.23.0's catalog pin.

